WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.120
Halloween 2018 has been a big hit with audiences
and critics alike, however, the movie almost

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.440
had a completely different ending and opening
scenes.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.369
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video I'm revealing Halloween's

00:00:13.369 --> 00:00:18.199
alternate ending and how the movie almost
changed the original film's finale!

00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:21.839
Make sure you watch to the end to also find
out all the other deleted scenes you never

00:00:21.839 --> 00:00:22.839
got to see!

00:00:22.839 --> 00:00:27.029
If you're new here, I do regular deep dives
into your favourite flicks, so make sure you

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:31.369
subscribe and also leave a comment about the
movie for a chance to win one of these cool

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:32.369
merch packs.

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.450
Spoilers ahead for Halloween, so take care
if you haven't seen the movie yet.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:41.550
The end of Halloween 2018 saw Laurie and the
Strode women trap Michael Myers in the basement

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:46.220
and burn the house down, leaving us with the
question of whether Michael survived.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:50.510
Originally though, the final confrontation
went down very differently but after it seems

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:54.710
test audiences reacted negatively, it was
completely reshot.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:59.770
In the alternate ending, Laurie ends up facing
off against Michael outside her house, rather

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:02.510
than inside the house as happens in the final
film.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:07.189
The deleted ending has Laurie trying to shoot
her tormentor but missing and then she finds

00:01:07.189 --> 00:01:08.759
she's run out of bullets.

00:01:08.759 --> 00:01:13.070
Michael has a kitchen knife, so Laurie pulls
out her hunting knife and charges at him.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:18.270
She slices him in the arm in a reverse of
what he did to her in the 1978 movie, but

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:21.659
Michael plunges his own knife into Laurie's
chest.

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:25.659
But just as he's about to kill Laurie off
with a final blow, her daughter Karen emerges

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:28.909
from the house and shoots Michael in the shoulder
with a crossbow.

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:33.210
Michael drops his knife which Allyson picks
up and the three women stagger away from the

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:34.210
house.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:38.330
Michael meanwhile is injured from the crossbow
arrow which has penetrated all the way through

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:41.619
his shoulder and he stumbles off into the
nearby wood.

00:01:41.619 --> 00:01:45.829
Laurie pleads with Karen and Allyson to kill
him, but her voice is too weak for them to

00:01:45.829 --> 00:01:46.829
hear.

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:51.240
After the women drive off in the truck, the
movie ends with Michael wandering into a clearing

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:55.380
filled with the creepy-looking mannequins
that Laurie uses for target practice.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.899
The script for this discarded ending then
states that Michael sits down by a tree and,

00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:03.149
exhausted, "his breathing deepens [… it's]
possibly his last".

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:07.959
Much of this ending was actually filmed as
you can see various scenes in the trailers

00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:10.679
and promo footage which never made it into
the final movie.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:15.120
And I can certainly see why it didn't test
so well with audiences as, in a number of

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.250
ways, it's not as satisfying as the ending
we did get.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:22.849
Firstly, by placing the ending outside, we
would have missed out on Michael pushing Laurie

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:27.360
off the balcony in a nice reverse of how he
fell off in the original movie.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.239
Secondly, Laurie's achievement of finally
trapping Michael in the safe room would never

00:02:31.239 --> 00:02:34.090
have happened, making her character arc not
as fulfilling.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.879
And thirdly, in the final film, burning down
the house also gives her an additional sense

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:40.930
of resolution and closure.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:45.209
And on top of that, the deleted ending makes
it more obvious that Michael is very likely

00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:50.079
still alive, whereas in the final film, it's
left open in a more interesting way.

00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:55.090
A few fans have said that even the ending
we did get felt a little abrupt, however,

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:59.379
this alternate ending sounds like it would
have been much shorter again and perhaps rather

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:01.360
anticlimactic.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.790
A major change that the Halloween 2018 filmmakers
almost made to the franchise's mythos is that

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:10.129
they very nearly altered the ending of the
first movie.

00:03:10.129 --> 00:03:14.439
Most shockingly, if the new filmmakers' had
gone ahead with their alternate ending to

00:03:14.439 --> 00:03:19.209
the original 1978 movie, we would have seen
Dr Loomis killed on screen!

00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:24.030
Fortunately, John Carpenter advised director
David Gordon Green not to do that as, in his

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:27.129
opinion, it would have really annoyed the
film's fans.

00:03:27.129 --> 00:03:31.849
Green had thought he needed to go back 40
years in his new film to remind people about

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:36.061
the ending to the first movie in case they'd
not seen it in a long time or were new to

00:03:36.061 --> 00:03:37.299
the franchise.

00:03:37.299 --> 00:03:41.750
And he planned to use his art director as
a body double for Donald Pleasence's Dr Loomis

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:45.400
because apparently, for the kind of shot they
were planning, he would have looked exactly

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.930
like the long deceased actor.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:52.129
As for young Laurie, she would have been recreated
using a blend of Jamie Lee Curtis and a young

00:03:52.129 --> 00:03:55.579
actress with a similar build to a 19-year
old Curtis.

00:03:55.579 --> 00:04:00.300
They also looked into digitally altering existing
footage from the original movie and I wonder

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:04.189
if they were thinking of doing something similar
to what Rogue One did with both Peter Cushing's

00:04:04.189 --> 00:04:06.859
character and a young Princess Leia?

00:04:06.859 --> 00:04:11.110
They were even going to cast one of the movie's
production assistants as a young Sheriff Hawkins

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:15.439
because he looked like a young Will Patton
who plays the present-day Hawkins!

00:04:15.439 --> 00:04:19.030
And that would have been filmed as part of
a scene showing Michael being captured by

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.030
the police.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:24.210
In the end, John Carpenter told them they
were making things way too complicated and

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:28.669
that the audience didn't need this extra scene
to get up to speed; so, instead there was

00:04:28.669 --> 00:04:33.590
just a single line of exposition from Dr Sartain
to Laurie when he explains that Hawkins was

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:38.110
"the first responding deputy [to arrive] when
Michael was arrested in 1978".

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:43.560
Interestingly, there's a little remnant of
this discarded reshoot idea in the final film.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:47.630
Look carefully at the room where Laurie and
Michael face off in the finale, and you'll

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:52.060
notice that it's a replica of the bedroom
from the end of the 1978 movie.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:56.250
The filmmakers had that set built to use for
their initial idea to reshoot the original

00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:01.000
film's climax; but when they decided against
that, they used the set anyway to keep down

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.530
the budget.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:06.780
And there's several additional deleted scenes
that ended up cut for pacing purposes.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.550
The first one comes just after Michael has
escaped from the prison bus.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:14.000
We cut to a shot of Dana, the British podcaster,
taking a shower.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.650
The bathroom door opens slowly and a masked
man pulls back the shower curtain.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:22.720
This scene was deliberately designed as an
homage to Alfred Hitchcock's Psycho, which

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:27.180
starred Jamie Lee Curtis's real-life mother
Janet Leigh in the iconic scene.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:31.599
The little twist though is that the masked
man isn’t actually Michael Myers, it's the

00:05:31.599 --> 00:05:34.810
other podcaster Aaron playing a prank on Dana.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:38.350
Aaron then takes the mask off, gives a line
about how wearing the mask or the legacy of

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:42.280
it inspires a certain tendency and then makes
out with Dana.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:46.430
Little fun fact now: Green's scrapped tribute
to Psycho would have been doubly fitting as

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:51.560
not only did Hitchcock's style influence John
Carpenter's original Halloween, but also Dr

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:54.990
Samuel Loomis was named after a character
from Psycho.

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:59.180
Curiously, Jamie Lee Curtis's mother [and
star of Psycho] Janet Leigh has previously

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:03.650
appeared in the Halloween franchise, playing
a secretary to her real-life daughter's character

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:05.000
in H20.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:09.300
In fact, that movie included a little easter
egg to Hitchcock's movie, with a shot of the

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:13.789
same car driven by Janet Leigh's character
in the 1960s classic.

00:06:13.789 --> 00:06:18.009
Another kill that was cut for pacing issues
is where Allyson was jogging and saw a dead

00:06:18.009 --> 00:06:20.569
dog strung upside down in a tree.

00:06:20.569 --> 00:06:24.370
It's not clear whether Michael killing the
dog was actually filmed, however, I suspect

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:26.330
it would have probably happened off screen.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:30.340
This moment would likely have been a little
hat-tip to the two dogs that Michael killed

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:34.819
in the 1978 film – the first of which was
never shown on screen; though we did partially

00:06:34.819 --> 00:06:38.639
see the death of the second dog Lester which
belonged to the little girl Laurie's friend

00:06:38.639 --> 00:06:39.639
Annie was babysitting.

00:06:39.639 --> 00:06:44.270
By the way, if you'd like to find out how
